{
 "name": "off-automatic-threshold-retains-tail-async-false",
 "description": "official-host.ts:830 'automatic threshold retains the effective recent projected tail without duplicating recovery (async=false)'. A resumed session (keepRecentTokens=1 globally, 30,000 for the model, window 335,000 / reserve 64,000) holds a discarded owner input, a 40k-char assistant message, a retained owner input, an omitted input (context_edit null) and a tool call whose result is replaced by a projected 80k receipt. Native preflight (estimated ~300k tokens) posthorse's recovery record keeps the projected tail (leading user anchor, retained owner, projected receipt, record AFTER the tail; omitted and unedited text never appear), no summary request is made, and history search finds nothing already in context. A second prompt on another model (per-model keepRecentTokens 25,000 stands in for the test's runtime override) hits an overflow again: the new record starts at the retained owner and does not nest the first.",
 "systemDiff": "hunks",
 "collapseRuns": 512,
 "model": {
  "id": "official-posthorse",
  "contextWindow": 335000,
  "maxTokens": 1000
 },
